  "narrative": "The due validations do not support the two context interactions they were testing. For H108, the culture-type adherent interaction on MSI-high/dependency_WRN was initially positive signed in discovery, +0.1046, 95% CI +0.037 to +0.172, but independent validation reversed and nullified the interaction, -0.0258, validation-adjusted CI -0.133 to +0.082. The validation interval excludes clinically meaningful positive interaction while including zero, so I reject H108 and close it. This does not threaten the robust main MSI-high/WRN association. For H38, the PIK3CA interaction on PTEN-loss/dependency_STAT3 was near null in discovery, +0.0013, CI -0.150 to +0.152, and validation was small and opposite signed, -0.0626, adjusted CI -0.252 to +0.127. PIK3CA status does not appear to modify the broader PTEN-loss/STAT3 association; H38 remains rejected and closed. I also converted several previously deferred null or small directional claims to closed rejects where their independent intervals do not plausibly support a clinically meaningful effect: KRAS-mutation gain in KRAS dependency, complete-QC KRAS-mutation KRAS dependency, adenocarcinoma-restricted KRAS and EGFR amplification probes, ERBB2-amplification/dependency_ERBB2, MDM2/TP53 and MDM2/MYC probes, WRN/BRCA2, and several narrow upper-bound null interactions. With these updates, the dataset-supported findings are the five large, repeated associations: SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, KEAP1 loss with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, MSI-high status with much stronger WRN dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, and TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency. These persist across matched-QC status, screen-quality strata, mutation-burden strata, CRISPR libraries, screen batches, culture subsets, and several specificity probes, with negligible or nonreplicated context interactions. Negative or unsupported findings now include canonical EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA/STAT3 under PTEN-intact context, PIK3CA modification of PTEN/STAT3, KRAS gain of KRAS dependency, MYC effects on DHX9/POLR2A/RPL11/USP7, RB1/KIF18A, ARID1A/SMARCA2, WRN/BRCA2, MDM2/TP53 or MDM2/MYC, and cross-driver receptor probes. Remaining uncertainty is mainly low-value or technically/culturally unresolved probes: TMED10 media-serum and MYC probes, research-marker F/STAT3, ERBB2 cross-driver and PIK3CA active probes, and some wide-null interactions where intervals cannot rule out a modest effect. The most informative next analysis is to complete the active media, marker, TMED10, and cross-driver probes plus the newly proposed complementary mutation-burden robustness tests. I request no new validation now; the two validation slots should be reserved unless an active probe produces a clinically meaningful point estimate with an interval that leaves ambiguity.",
  "research_notes": "Round 10 synthesis: assessed two due validations. H108 discovery interaction +0.105 was not replicated; validation -0.026 with adjusted CI -0.133 to +0.082, reject/close. H38 PIK3CA interaction null in discovery and opposite/null in validation; keep reject/close. Converted many small or null unresolved claims to closed reject because their 95% intervals do not support clinically meaningful directional effects, including H1 KRAS/dependency_KRAS, H134 complete-QC KRAS/dependency_KRAS, H4 ERBB2 amplification/dependency_ERBB2, H6/H79/H101 MDM2 probes, H18 adenocarcinoma EGFR amplification/dependency_EGFR, H21 WRN/BRCA2, H22 adenocarcinoma KRAS mutation, H57, H104, and H111 null interactions. Accepted evidence base remains SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency; MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; PTEN-loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency; TP53-loss -> weaker USP7 dependency. These are dataset-specific associations, robust to QC, screen quality, mutation burden, library, batch, and culture subsets, but not causal or externally generalizable claims. Negative findings now include KRAS gain, EGFR/ERBB2 amplification main and cross-driver probes, PIK3CA STAT3 effect under PTEN-intact context, MYC dependency probes, RB1/KIF18A, ARID1A/SMARCA2, WRN/BRCA2, MDM2 probes, and most context interactions. Unresolved/deferred: some wide interaction nulls where upper bounds near 0.1 remain; no-evidence subgroup main effects; active probes H116 TMED10 media, H117 marker F STAT3, H130 TMED10 MYC, H132/H136/H137 receptor/PIK3CA probes. Registered four mutation-burden complement robustness tests: USP7/TP53 in lower TMB, SMARCA2/SMARCA4 in higher TMB, NFE2L2/KEAP1 in higher TMB, STAT3/PTEN in lower TMB. No validation requested; keep two slots in reserve."
}

