  "research_notes": "Iteration 14 appraise complete. Twelve new discovery claims were assessed and all were rejected as unsupported: new predictor probes (MSI/DHX9, MYC/MDM2, TP53/RPL11, RB1/RPL11, NF1/RIT1, SMAD4/STAT3, KEAP1/DHX9), interaction probes (MYC modifying PTEN-loss STAT3; PTEN co-loss modifying TP53-loss USP7), and specificity controls (SMARCA4/NFE2L2, PTEN/USP7, marker F/STAT3). The accepted claim set is unchanged. These nulls strengthen, but do not prove, outcome and context specificity of accepted large associations: MSI-high appears WRN-specific among tested dependencies; KEAP1 loss appears strongly NFE2L2-specific; SMARCA4 loss appears strongly SMARCA2-specific; PTEN loss appears STAT3-specific among tested outcomes; TP53 loss appears USP7-specific among tested outcomes. Remaining validation capacity: one unused new voluntary validation request. Active remaining probes include H166 low-burden SMARCA2 context, H180 marker E/USP7 specificity, H185-H188 cross controls, H189 EMT modifier, H190 proliferation modifier, H194 PIK3CA TP53-wt STAT3, and H198 TP53/SMARCA2. If these remain null, they further support specificity and context robustness; only a large precise effect well beyond the null and accepted-interaction noise should trigger a new association, scope-narrowing interaction, or validation request."
