  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation capacity is exhausted, so the scientifically useful next step is internal refinement: test whether the already accepted core dependency associations persist under biologically and technically distinct conditions, and test whether the only accepted effect modification is robust to a higher IFN_gamma threshold. The first two proposals refine the accepted IFN-high amplification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency by using a stricter top-quantile-like IFN threshold of ifn_gamma_signature >= 0.6 instead of >= 0.5. The direct contrast tests whether the raw PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency difference remains strongly negative in this high-IFN subset; the interaction tests whether that subset-specific difference remains more negative than in the complement. Both use direction -1, so a positive signed estimate corresponds to stronger, more negative STAT3 dependency in the registered direction.\n\nThe next five proposals test the five accepted core associations in a high-ploidy context, ploidy >= 3.0. Ploidy is a distinct genome-state measure from aneuploidy_score, chromosomal instability proxies, mutation burden, screen QC, growth rate, and previously tested interaction contexts. The expectations are persistence of the same signs: SMARCA4 loss remains associated with more negative SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1 loss remains associated with less negative NFE2L2 dependency; MSI-high remains associated with more negative WRN dependency; PTEN loss remains associated with more negative STAT3 dependency; and TP53 loss remains associated with less negative USP7 dependency. These tests are important because rare-exposure cells could become imprecise or directionally distorted in high-ploidy lines, especially for MSI-high and PTEN loss, but median-like high-ploidy groups should still retain at least 20 exposed and comparator cells for these predictors.\n\nThe final five proposals test the same five core associations only in low-serum culture conditions, media_serum_pct == 5.0. Low serum is a culture-context perturbation that can affect proliferation and cell state, and it was not used for the main core-association robustness program. Direct contrasts within the 5% serum subset test whether each association persists when media context is restricted, rather than merely comparing high versus low serum or performing an interaction. Again, the expected signed results are positive under the registered directions if the established associations persist.\n\nAll new claims remain dataset-specific associations, not causal claims. Acceptance will require the signed estimate to be in the registered direction, the 95% Welch interval to exclude zero, all comparison cells to satisfy the minimum-n rule, and the magnitude to be scientifically meaningful relative to the practical 10% benchmark or comparable to the already accepted core effects. Near-zero or interval-crossing results should be interpreted as failure to support the registered effect or persistence claim in that dataset, not proof of absence. Interaction results should support context amplification only if the signed interaction is precise and non-null.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 19 explore. Validation capacity is exhausted. Core accepted dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H5/R5 +0.784; validation R39 +0.800); KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency, registered reverse claim (H17/R7 +0.796; validation R13 +0.801); MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (H8/R8 +0.790; validation R52 +0.807); PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency (H14/R15 +0.267; validation R26 +0.310); TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency (H12/R12 +0.396; validation R65 +0.395). Accepted borderline internal effect modification: IFN-high amplifies PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency (H228/R216 direct +0.428; H231/R219 interaction +0.221). Many driver and cross-driver probes rejected, including KRAS-KRAS, BRAF-BRAF/KRAS/EGFR/ERBB2, EGFR-EGFR, ERBB2-ERBB2, MYC broad probes, culture/EMT/mutation-burden/culture-MSI-WRN modifiers, and most tested research markers. Unresolved/deferred claims remain untested and do not support conclusions. Iteration 19 registers 12 internal probes: IFN top-quantile direct and interaction refinement of PTEN-STAT3 amplification; high-ploidy robustness for five core associations; 5% serum robustness for five core associations. Analyze should prioritize IFN threshold robustness plus core persistence in ploidy and low-serum contexts. Interpret accepted results only as associations in this dataset, not causal mechanisms or generalizable claims."
