  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered results are signed to the registered hypothesis directions and every comparison cell satisfies the minimum-observation rule. H242 and H243 strengthen the previously identified IFN-high effect modification of the PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency association. At the stricter threshold ifn_gamma_signature >= 0.6, the direct PTEN-loss contrast is +0.452 [0.347, 0.556], indicating substantially stronger STAT3 dependency in the high-IFN PTEN-loss group, while the formal interaction is +0.243 [0.124, 0.362]. Both intervals exclude zero and are above the practical 0.1 magnitude benchmark. I therefore accept both as dataset-specific support for IFN-associated amplification of the PTEN-loss STAT3 association. This remains an internal, threshold-dependent finding: the 0.6 cutoff is close to the earlier 0.5 cutoff, the IFN score is dichotomized, and multiple IFN-related contrasts have now been examined, so confidence is moderate rather than strong and external/generalizable causal claims are not supported. H244-H248 test the five core accepted associations in high-ploidy lines (ploidy >= 3.0). All five persist with signed estimates excluding zero: SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 +0.762 [0.726, 0.798]; KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 +0.802 [0.763, 0.842]; MSI-high/WRN +0.788 [0.732, 0.844]; PTEN-loss/STAT3 +0.243 [0.145, 0.341]; and TP53-loss/USP7 +0.272 [0.127, 0.417]. The magnitudes are either very large or exceed the 0.1 practical benchmark, and the intervals exclude zero. H249-H253 test the same five core associations in low-serum culture (media_serum_pct = 5). All again persist: SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 +0.766 [0.726, 0.805]; KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 +0.788 [0.747, 0.829]; MSI-high/WRN +0.779 [0.711, 0.848]; PTEN-loss/STAT3 +0.214 [0.114, 0.313]; and TP53-loss/USP7 +0.268 [0.108, 0.428]. These are internal stratified robustness tests using overlapping cell-line data, not independent external replications, and should not be overinterpreted as independent confirmations. Nevertheless, they provide consistent evidence that the accepted core associations are not driven by a single ploidy or serum-context subgroup. Because independent validation capacity is exhausted, no validation was requested. These conclusions remain associations in the supplied lung-derived CRISPR dataset, not causal mechanisms or externally generalizable claims.",
