  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered discovery analyses have valid minimum cell counts, and the estimates are interpreted as already signed to the registered hypothesis directions. The IFN specificity probes are scientifically informative: the formal high-IFN interaction tests for SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 (H263, R254: -0.027 [-0.071,0.016]), MSI-high/WRN (H264, R255: +0.024 [-0.036,0.084]), TP53 loss/USP7 (H265, R256: -0.044 [-0.218,0.130]), and KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2 (H271, R257: -0.006 [-0.052,0.040]) are all imprecise or near-null and cross the no-effect region. Their point estimates are far below the practical 10% benchmark. I therefore reject these interaction claims as unsupported in this dataset. Together with the accepted high-IFN PTEN-loss/STAT3 interactions, these nulls support the narrower dataset-specific conclusion that IFN_gamma_signature effect modification is specific to the PTEN-loss/STAT3 association among the tested core effects. The lower-threshold IFN>=0.4 MSI-high/WRN interaction (H275, R261: +0.015 [-0.044,0.075]) is also null despite better cell counts, further weakening any broad WRN-MSI/IFN modification hypothesis. The direct effects in IFN-high strata remain large and robust: KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2 (H272, R258: +0.792 [0.752,0.831]), TP53 loss/USP7 (H273, R259: +0.363 [0.208,0.518]), and SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 (H274, R260: +0.764 [0.727,0.801]). All exclude zero and exceed the practical magnitude threshold, so I accept them as internal evidence that the core associations persist in IFN-high subsets. These are not new effect-modification claims. The MYC amplification interaction on KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2 (H266, R262: -0.008 [-0.072,0.057]) is null, supporting absence of MYC amplification as a modifier of that association. The genetic-context tests are also decisive: ARID1A loss among SMARCA4-wildtype lines has no meaningful SMARCA2 association (H267, R263: -0.003 [-0.025,0.019]), supporting SMARCA4-specificity rather than broad PBAF/ARID1A-related synthetic lethality in this dataset. MSI-high remains strongly associated with WRN dependency among BRCA2-wildtype lines (H268, R264: +0.794 [0.764,0.825]), whereas BRCA2 loss has no association among MSI-negative lines (H269, R265: +0.001 [-0.031,0.032]). This separates the WRN finding from BRCA2-loss synthetic-lethal hypotheses and supports MSI-high as the relevant marker in this dataset. Overall, the new evidence strengthens the accepted core associations and the IFN-specific PTEN/STAT3 modifier, while rejecting the broader IFN, MYC, ARID1A, and BRCA2 modification hypotheses. These remain associations in the supplied dataset only; multiple thresholded IFN tests and dichotomization limit generalizability and causal interpretation. Independent validation capacity is exhausted, so no validation request is made.",
