  "narrative": "No new validation result or response deadline is listed for this synthesis, and independent validation capacity is exhausted, so I consolidate the existing evidence and make no validation request. The strongest, internally robust, signed associations in the supplied dataset are five marker-to-dependency relationships whose magnitudes exceed the 10% practical benchmark and are internally consistent across many eligibility strata. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency: signed discovery +0.784 [0.765, 0.803] on R5 and independent validation +0.800 [0.768, 0.832] on R39. Second, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency: signed discovery +0.796 [0.776, 0.816] on R7 and validation +0.801 [0.772, 0.829] on R13. Third, MSI-high status is associated with stronger WRN dependency: signed discovery +0.790 [0.760, 0.819] on R8 and validation +0.807 [0.759, 0.855] on R52. Fourth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: signed discovery +0.267 [0.215, 0.319] on R15 and validation +0.310 [0.231, 0.388] on R26. Fifth, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency: signed discovery +0.396 [0.325, 0.467] on R12 and validation +0.395 [0.293, 0.497] on R65. These are dataset-specific associations, not causal or external biological claims. The only supported effect modification is high interferon context amplifying the PTEN-loss STAT3-dependency association. Direct PTEN-loss contrasts persist in IFN-high strata: IFN >= 0.5 signed +0.428 [0.326, 0.529] on R216, IFN >= 0.6 +0.452 [0.347, 0.556] on R230, and IFN >= 0.8 +0.436 [0.308, 0.565] on R242. Formal interactions are supported at the same moderate-to-high thresholds: +0.221 [0.104, 0.338] on R219, +0.243 [0.124, 0.362] on R231, and +0.200 [0.060, 0.339] on R243. By contrast, the extreme IFN >= 1.0 interaction is unsupported at +0.083 [-0.091, 0.257] on R246, and the low-IFN tail interaction at IFN <= -0.75 is unsupported at +0.127 [-0.010, 0.264] on R248. The low-IFN direct contrasts remain positive but smaller, for example +0.138 [0.041, 0.235] on R244 and +0.162 [0.037, 0.286] on R247. Thus, if this dataset is summarized as a whole, IFN appears to amplify PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency at thresholds around 0.5 to 0.8, while the modification is not robust at the extreme high tail and is not supported as a low-tail interaction. Importantly, this effect modification is specific to PTEN-loss STAT3 among the tested core effects: high-IFN interaction tests for SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2, MSI-high WRN, TP53-loss USP7, and KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 are all null or imprecise, R254 -0.027 [-0.071, 0.016], R255 +0.024 [-0.036, 0.084], R256 -0.044 [-0.218, 0.130], and R257 -0.006 [-0.052, 0.040]. The lower-threshold WRN IFN interaction is also null at +0.015 [-0.044, 0.075] on R261. MYC amplification does not modify KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependency, R262 -0.008 [-0.072, 0.057]. The new context tests also strengthen marker specificity: ARID1A loss among SMARCA4-wildtype lines is null for SMARCA2, R263 -0.003 [-0.025, 0.019], supporting SMARCA4-specific association rather than a broad ARID1A synthetic-lethal effect. MSI-high remains strongly associated with WRN dependency among BRCA2-wildtype lines, R264 +0.794 [0.764, 0.825], while BRCA2 loss among MSI-negative lines is null, R265 +0.001 [-0.031, 0.032], supporting MSI-high rather than BRCA2-loss as the relevant marker in this dataset. Major negative findings are scientifically useful. KRAS mutation does not support KRAS, RIT1, BRAF, or STAT3 dependency hypotheses; BRAF V600E does not support BRAF, KRAS, EGFR, ERBB2, or RIT1 dependency hypotheses; EGFR amplification is rejected and has discordant discovery/validation behavior on R3 and R119; ERBB2 amplification does not support ERBB2 or TMED10 dependency hypotheses. TP53 loss explains USP7 dependency but not MDM2, STAT3, SMARCA2, WRN, or RPL11 dependencies. MYC amplification shows no broad association across the tested dependency outcomes. The constructed research markers D/E/F are null where tested. Most interaction hypotheses are rejected, including lineage, culture, screen quality, PIK3CA, KEAP1, MYC, EMT, mutation-burden, ploidy, IFN for non-STAT3 outcomes, and BRCA2-specificity tests. Remaining uncertainty is substantial. The accepted findings are associations in this supplied dataset only; causal mechanisms are not established. Independent validation is limited mostly to the core marker outcomes, and IFN thresholding was explored across multiple cutoffs, so the IFN-specific PTEN/STAT3 modification could be sensitive to post-hoc dichotomization. Some deferred or active comparisons remain untested, including the IFN >= 0.7 direct and interaction probes H276 and H277. The most informative next analysis would be to evaluate IFN >= 0.7 if cell-size rules are met and, ideally, replace thresholded IFN analyses with continuous or spline-based IFN modeling with covariate adjustment for PTEN-loss STAT3 interaction. If that does not change the conclusion, the final scientific position is: five robust dataset-specific marker-dependency associations, and one supported threshold-dependent effect modifier, high IFN amplification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency, with broad support for nullity of other tested driver, marker, and interaction hypotheses.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis with no new validation and no validation capacity. Supported core associations: SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2 (R5/R39); KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2 (R7/R13, plus IFN-high R258); MSI-high -> stronger WRN (R8/R52, plus BRCA2-wildtype R264); PTEN-loss -> stronger STAT3 (R15/R26); TP53-loss -> weaker USP7 (R12/R65). Supported effect modification: high IFN amplifies PTEN-loss/STAT3 at IFN >= 0.5, 0.6, 0.8 (R216/R219, R230/R231, R242/R243); not supported at IFN >= 1.0 interaction R246 or low tail interaction R248. IFN modification is specific to PTEN/STAT3 because non-STAT3 core IFN interactions are null (R254, R255, R256, R257, R261). Marker specificity: ARID1A null in SMARCA4-wildtype (R263); MSI-high WRN persists in BRCA2-wildtype (R264), BRCA2 loss null in MSI-negative (R265); MYC does not modify KEAP1/NFE2L2 (R262). Negative findings: KRAS/BRAF/EGFR/ERBB2 driver hypotheses null or rejected; TP53 loss not MDM2/STAT3/SMARCA2/WRN/RPL11; MYC broad null; D/E/F markers null; most interactions null. Limitations: dataset-specific, no causal inference, IFN thresholds post-hoc, sparse strata, limited external validation. Next best analysis: run active IFN >= 0.7 H276/H277 if valid, preferably with continuous/spline IFN interaction and covariate adjustment."
