  "narrative": "All twelve new discovery results have valid Welch diagnostics and satisfy the minimum cell-size rule, and estimates are interpreted as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. H276 provides strong internal evidence that the PTEN-loss STAT3-dependency association persists in the IFN_gamma_signature >= 0.7 stratum: signed +0.447, 95% CI 0.335 to 0.559, well above the practical 0.10 benchmark. H277 formally supports effect modification in the same stratum: interaction +0.222, 95% CI 0.097 to 0.347. This fills the previously untested 0.7 threshold and is consistent with the accepted IFN >= 0.5, >= 0.6, and >= 0.8 interactions, while the extreme IFN >= 1.0 interaction remains unsupported. Because these IFN thresholds are overlapping and thresholded, the accepted IFN modification should remain a cautious dataset-specific association rather than a precise mechanistic threshold claim, but the pattern supports moderate-high IFN contexts amplifying PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency. H278-H282 robustly replicate the five core marker-dependency associations in the higher-Cas9-activity stratum: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency +0.788, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency +0.776, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency +0.257, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency +0.800, and TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency +0.390; all CIs exclude zero. These are not new independent causal effects, but they strengthen technical plausibility that the associations are not obviously artifacts of poor editing in this dataset. H283 accepts a direct PTEN-loss STAT3 association in hypoxia >= 0.5: +0.251, CI 0.149 to 0.352. However, H284 rejects hypoxia as an amplifier of the STAT3 association: interaction -0.0235, CI -0.141 to 0.094. H285 rejects a hypoxia interaction for KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependency: -0.0225, CI -0.070 to 0.025. H286 and H287 reject high MYC mRNA abundance as an interaction context for KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 (+0.0297, CI -0.028 to 0.087) and SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 (+0.0188, CI -0.039 to 0.076), both near zero and below the practical benchmark. I accept the direct stratum results as internal robustness evidence and reject the interaction/modifier hypotheses as unsupported. No validation request is made because independent validation capacity is exhausted. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable biological claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported dataset-specific conclusions after appraise iteration 22: five core marker-dependency associations remain robust: SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency; PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency; TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency. New Cas9_activity_score >= 1.0 direct strata accept all five core associations, supporting internal robustness and reducing concern that these are simple artifacts of poor editing context, though still not causal evidence. IFN_gamma_signature effect modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 is supported at >= 0.5, >= 0.6, >= 0.7, and >= 0.8; the new >= 0.7 direct effect R266 is +0.447 and interaction R267 is +0.222. Extreme IFN >= 1.0 interaction remains unsupported, low-tail interaction unsupported, and IFN modification is not supported for other core outcomes at tested thresholds. Thus IFN appears to be a specific moderate-high threshold modifier for PTEN-loss STAT3 in this dataset, but the finding remains vulnerable to dichotomization and multiple-threshold exploration. Hypoxia direct STAT3 association persists, but hypoxia does not modify STAT3 or NFE2L2 associations. High MYC mRNA abundance does not modify NFE2L2 or SMARCA2 associations. Broad driver/amplification hypotheses for KRAS, BRAF, EGFR, and ERBB2 remain unsupported, as do many lineage, culture, screen-quality, mutation-burden, ploidy, genetic-specificity, and research-marker comparisons. Validation capacity is exhausted; no further validation requested. Remaining scientific uncertainty is mainly generalizability and whether thresholded IFN modification would be better represented by continuous modeling, but no independent validation budget remains."
