  "narrative": "All twelve final discovery contrasts are valid Welch comparisons and every cell meets the 20-observation minimum. Estimates and intervals are interpreted as already signed to the registered directions. H312 and H313 accept direct PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency associations in non-overlapping IFN bins: [0.4,0.8) gives +0.362 (95% CI 0.217 to 0.507) and [-0.749,0.399] gives +0.221 (95% CI 0.151 to 0.290). These support persistence of the PTEN association across moderate-to-high and lower/middle IFN ranges, with a rough gradient rather than a sharp threshold. H314 accepts the high-Cas9, IFN<=0.399 direct association, +0.164 (95% CI 0.082 to 0.246), though the lower bound falls below the practical 0.10 benchmark, so acceptance is cautious; H315 accepts the lower-Cas9, IFN<=0.399 association, +0.348 (95% CI 0.219 to 0.477), showing that the PTEN effect does not require high Cas9 activity. H316-H320 accept all five core marker-dependency associations in the low-ploidy complement: SMARCA4 loss to SMARCA2 dependency +0.792, KEAP1 loss to weaker NFE2L2 dependency +0.794, MSI-high to WRN dependency +0.790, TP53 loss to weaker USP7 dependency +0.443, and PTEN loss to STAT3 dependency +0.277. These are large relative to the benchmark and add dataset-specific robustness, not generalizability. H321 accepts a low-ploidy IFN>=0.5 interaction for PTEN-loss STAT3, +0.212 (95% CI 0.069 to 0.354), but its lower bound is below 0.10 and exposed cells are modest, so it should be treated as a cautious indication of the same rough context gradient rather than precise effect modification. H322 accepts a strong direct PTEN-loss STAT3 association in the 10% serum, IFN>=0.5 context, +0.457 (95% CI 0.321 to 0.593). H323 rejects ARID1A loss as a meaningful SMARCA2 association among SMARCA4-wildtype low-ploidy lines, signed -0.00016 (95% CI -0.026 to 0.026), supporting marker specificity of the SMARCA4-SMARCA2 result. Multiplicity and observational confounding remain important: IFN, Cas9, ploidy, media, and molecular context are correlated, and this is a large exploration without new independent validation capacity. The conclusions therefore remain dataset-specific associations and robustness checks, not causal effects or claims about other screens or populations.",
